 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Shark NZ801UK anti hair wrap upright - suction has gone really weak over the last couple of weeks, barely picks up crumbs. Have emptied the bin. Any ideas before I buy a new one?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Yes, please hold off on buying a new one as weak suction is almost always fixable and rarely means the motor has failed. Since you’ve emptied the bin, the next most common cause is a clogged filter that needs time to dry out properly. Please wash the pre-motor and HEPA filters in cold water only and leave them somewhere warm for at least 24 hours until they are completely bone-dry. A damp filter severely chokes airflow, so please do not put it back in until you are sure it is fully dry.\n[Helpful to see: image \"Poor suction — what to check first\" — Lost suction is usually a full bin, a dirty filter or a blockage in the hose, tube or floor head — check and clear those before suspecting the motor. Switch off and unplug first. Typical layout — your model may differ.]"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Found the foam and felt filters under the bin, never washed them before. Washed them and left them 24 hours. Suction is back to like new, big difference. No burning smell or cutting out at any point, by the way."
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "That’s excellent news! I’m really glad to hear the suction is back to like new after washing those filters. To keep it running smoothly, just remember to check and wash them every few months or whenever you notice a drop in performance. Is there anything else I can help you with today?"
  }
 ],
